            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0361" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">358.116 M 82/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-02T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1921—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:80 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. The Swedish Government has recently assumed an unfriendly attitude toward the
                    missionaries of the Mormon Church in Sweden and has to date ordered the
                    expulsion of 4 of the 11 American missionaries here as was done in 1914. See my
                    number 8, September 17th.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d190-f1"/> At the instance of
                    Mr. Oscar W. Soderberg, vice president of this church in Sweden, I took the
                    matter up with the Foreign Minister who informed me that the case had been
                    decided in Crown Council meeting and that the attitude of the Government on this
                    point was firm. However, at my request he would allow Mr. Soderberg himself to
                    remain a month to wind up the affairs of the church here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
